'''Amphipnoina''' (am-fip-nō-ī′nä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''Amphipnous'' + ''-ina.''] The ''Amphipnoidæ'', as a subfamily of ''Symbranchiidæ'', having the vent in the posterior half of the skull, and the scapular arch not attached to the skull. ''Günther.'' Also written ''Amphipnoinæ.''

